    "text": "Instead of seeing a full case upfront, Microsoft's MAI-DxO asks follow-up questions and selects tests step by step. In a newly published Science study, it scored 83% on complex teaching cases versus 36% for generalist doctors using references. The catch: a controlled, text-only benchmark isn't evidence of better real-world patient care. Prospective hospital testing is next.",
